test/check/error-primes.sumspec:8:18:
  |
8 | onSource :: App(A') -> App(A)
  |                  ^
a prime (') marks a new value, so it can only be on the target side

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:9:23:
  |
9 | twice :: App -> App(A'')
  |                       ^
a name takes at most one prime (')

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:10:33:
   |
10 | onPath :: Page.Home -> Page.Plan'
   |                                 ^
a prime (') goes only on a bare type name such as Missions'; a written variant or argument already says what the new value is

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:11:40:
   |
11 | onArgs :: Page.Home -> Page.Plan(A * B)'
   |                                        ^
a prime (') goes only on a bare type name such as Missions'; a written variant or argument already says what the new value is

test/check/error-primes.sumspec:12:37:
   |
12 | onList :: Page.Home -> Page.Many([B]')
   |                                     ^
a prime (') goes only on a bare type name such as Missions'; a written variant or argument already says what the new value is

